    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I need both CI/CD and IaC?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "They work best together: IaC defines infra; CI/CD deploys code and infrastructure safely and repeatably."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I roll back quickly?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Use blue/green or canary releases with health\u2011based automated rollback."
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>


<h1 id="primary-question">How do CI/CD and Infrastructure as Code reduce risk and speed delivery?</h1>
<p class="answer lead">CI/CD automates build, test, and deploy with approvals and rollbacks; IaC makes environments reproducible and reviewable. Together they standardize changes, catch issues earlier, and shorten recovery. Use branch protection, policy‑as‑code checks, and staged releases (blue/green or canary).</p>
